{"name":"Carriage Wheel","hex":"#5d6367","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"carriage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of conveying; carrying.","A means of conveyance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carriage"},{"term":"wheel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A circular device capable of rotating on its axis, facilitating movement or transportation or performing labour in machines.\n\n A steering wheel and its implied control of a vehicle.","A steering wheel and its implied control of a vehicle."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To roll along on wheels.","To transport something or someone using any wheeled mechanism, such as a wheelchair."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wheel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carriage","blocks":[{"text":"A carriage is a two- or four-wheeled horse-drawn vehicle for passengers. Coaches are a special category within carriages; they are enclosed carriages with four corner posts and a fixed roof. From the early modern period until the rise of railways and motor vehicles, carriages were a principal means of road transport, with models ranging from simple vehicles to elaborate ceremonial coaches used by royalty. Although largely replaced by mechanized transport, carriages remain in use for ceremonial occasions, tourism, equestrian sport, and in some communities as everyday transport. Modern carriages have been redesigned and manufactured for sports such as combined driving and for tourist transport."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Horse_of_Buckingham_Palace%2C_Londres_cropped_straightened.jpg/330px-Horse_of_Buckingham_Palace%2C_Londres_cropped_straightened.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carriage","wikidata":"Q235356"},{"title":"Wheel","blocks":[{"text":"A wheel is a rotating component intended to turn on an axle bearing. The wheel is one of the key components of the wheel and axle, which is one of the six simple machines. Wheels, in conjunction with axles, allow heavy objects to be moved easily, facilitating transportation, supporting loads, and performing work in machines. Wheels are also used for other purposes, such as a ship's wheel, steering wheel, potter's wheel, and flywheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Landesmuseum_W%C3%BCrttemberg_Kelten_011.4.jpg/330px-Landesmuseum_W%C3%BCrttemberg_Kelten_011.4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wheel","wikidata":"Q446"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Concours_national_d%27attelage_%C3%A9lite_Rennes_2014-1.jpg/500px-Concours_national_d%27attelage_%C3%A9lite_Rennes_2014-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Concours_national_d%27attelage_%C3%A9lite_Rennes_2014-1.jpg/1280px-Concours_national_d%27attelage_%C3%A9lite_Rennes_2014-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Concours_national_d%27attelage_%C3%A9lite_Rennes_2014-1.jpg/500px-Concours_national_d%27attelage_%C3%A9lite_Rennes_2014-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Competitive driving in France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AConcours_national_d'attelage_%C3%A9lite_Rennes_2014-1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Sal%C3%A3o_Nobre%2C_Museu_Nacional_dos_Coches%2C_Lisboa%2C_Portugal.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Sal%C3%A3o_Nobre%2C_Museu_Nacional_dos_Coches%2C_Lisboa%2C_Portugal.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Sal%C3%A3o_Nobre%2C_Museu_Nacional_dos_Coches%